  "demo_v5_text": "Loss of $512.02 on 1 lot = massive overrun. SL at 4,368.13 vs entry 4,373.64 = 4.51 pips, but real exit at 4,367.7 = 5.94 pips. The USD loss amount is excessive.",
  "demo_v6_rule": "Unauthorized pair",
  "demo_v6_text": "Trade on US100.CASH while only XAUUSD is authorized. Direct violation of the authorized pairs rule.",
  "demo_v7_rule": "Loss exceeding maximum SL of 75 pips",
  "demo_v7_text": "Loss of $476.93 on 0.5 lot. SL at 4,963.15 vs entry 4,963.70 = entry outside strategic zone. No visible BOS/confirmation.",
  "demo_v8_rule": "Loss exceeding maximum SL of 75 pips",
  "demo_v8_text": "Loss of $703.39 on 0.5 lot. Entry 5,331.22, exit 5,334.83 = 16.39 pips, but no valid ICT structure. No confirmed entry FVG.",
  "demo_p1_type": "Chronic Revenge Trading",
  "demo_p1_text": "3 major episodes: (1) Feb 19 = 3 long trades within hours after a losing streak, (2) Mar 9 = 3 trades in 30 seconds with cumulative losses of $675, (3) Apr 2-4 = 2 near-identical long trades 25 seconds apart. After each loss, immediate increase in entries.",
  "demo_p2_type": "Massive Overtrading",
  "demo_p2_text": "54 out of 80 trades (67.5%) are overtrading: either rapid entries in the same zone (5-30 seconds) or excessive daily accumulations (3 trades Mar 18, 5 trades Apr 16). Lot reduced to 0.05-0.3 indicates inappropriate scalping for an ICT strategy.",
  "demo_p3_type": "Lot Size Increase After Losses",
  "demo_p3_text": "After $512 loss (Jan 2), lot increased to 1.5 (Jan 16). After $476 loss (Feb 4), lot oscillates between 0.3-1. Micro-lots (0.05) after huge losses suggest accumulated panic.",
  "demo_p4_type": "Failure to Respect ICT Structure",
  "demo_p4_text": "Most trades miss one or more ICT setup steps: no liquidity rejection confirmation, unvalidated FVG, no Break of Structure, entries without waiting for valid retracement. Only 26 compliant trades out of 80.",
  "demo_p5_type": "Unauthorized Pairs Violation",
  "demo_p5_text": "3 trades on unauthorized pairs: US100.CASH (Jan 7), USDJPY (Mar 30), BTCUSD (Apr 15). Off-strategy trading = 3.75% of trades in direct violation.",
  "demo_p6_type": "Compulsive Lot Scaling Down",
  "demo_p6_text": "Lot progression: 1 → 0.5 → 0.3 → 0.25 → 0.2 → 0.15 → 0.05. When trades lose, instead of stopping, the trader reduces lot size and continues. Panic masked as 'risk management'.",
  "demo_s1": "You identified 26 ICT-compliant trades (32%): Jan 11-12 trades (+$1,070), Mar 30 short (+$1,180), and Mar 18-19 longs (+$474 each) show solid understanding when discipline is applied. When you follow your strategy, RR ratios are excellent.",
  "demo_s2": "The 75-pip maximum SL limit is generally respected in real pip terms (most losses = USD overrun, not pips). Physical stop losses are correctly positioned when used.",
  "demo_s3": "You recognized the need to reduce lot sizes after losses (moving from 1.5 to 0.3-0.05), showing risk awareness. Without this adaptation, the damage would have been far worse.",
  "demo_reco_1": "IMPERATIVE: Implement a pause after 3 consecutive losing trades. You already have this rule in your strategy but don't apply it. Mar 9 (3 trades in 30 sec), Feb 19 (3 losing trades in a row) should have triggered an automatic stop. After the 3rd loss, leave the platform for at least 2 hours.",
  "demo_reco_2": "CRITICAL: Enforce a minimum 30-60 minute delay between entries on the same pair. Your ICT setup requires: liquidity → sweep → rejection → retracement → FVG. That takes market time. You cannot have 3 valid setups in 30 seconds. Ask: 'Have I identified NEW liquidity?' If not, entry is FORBIDDEN.",
  "demo_reco_3": "URGENT: Validate that EVERY trade respects all 9 setup steps before clicking BUY/SELL. Mandatory checklist: ☐ Liquidity identified ☐ Sweep confirmed ☐ Clear rejection ☐ Valid retracement ☐ Break of Structure ☐ FVG formed ☐ Entry IN the FVG ☐ Confirmation waited ☐ Structure not trapped. ONE empty box = do NOT enter.",
